ion related to tumors can produce symptoms. This frames blood testing as a means to identify endocrine activity or paraneoplastic phenomena that may require additional evaluation. [Data: Entities (316)]\\n\\nA relationship explicitly states that blood tests are used to look for signs of hormone secretion, tying the broad BLOOD TESTS hub to endocrine-functional assessment beyond thyroid-specific monitoring. This expands the community’s scope from hematologic monitoring and tumor markers into endocrine tumor evaluation signals. [Data: Entities (156, 316); Relationships (394)]\"}],\"rating\":3.2,\"rating_explanation\":\"The community reflects medically standard and widely used oncology testing/monitoring practices with high clinical importance but no inherent indication of illicit activity or harmful intent in the provided data. [Data: Entities (156, 2952, 5137, 1458); Relationships (5607, 2899, 11352, 2385, 9371,+more)]\"}", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, "provider_specific_fields": {"native_finish_reason": "stop"}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1792, "prompt_tokens": 4155, "total_tokens": 5947, "completion_tokens_details": {"accepted_prediction_tokens": null, "audio_tokens": null, "reasoning_tokens": 0, "rejected_prediction_tokens": null, "text_tokens": null}, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1664, "text_tokens": null, "image_tokens": null}}, "service_tier": null}}}